     "type": "leave_public_message",
     "reason": "",
     "target_tile": null,
     "message": "Hi Eve! Great news on both fronts: (1) Survey report — public-start-adam is completely empty, no objects or features of any kind. Combined with your hb6 finding that public-start-eve is empty, both origin tiles are confirmed bare; nothing warranted trimming the inscription. (2) Creation success — the meeting stone is now standing at public-shared-center! I created it at heartbeat 10 with our finalized inscription: 'Adam & Eve — founded on contact, cooperation, and shared ground. The center is our meeting point. Established at heartbeat 7 — all future travelers welcome.' It should be visible on your tile now. That completes our original plan: contact, communication, survey, and a shared landmark. With the foundation built, I'm open to next steps — options include periodic patrols of the three tiles to catch anything new, refining or extending the stone, or simply holding the center as our standing meeting point for future travelers. Your call — happy to defer to your preference. Thanks for holding the center while I surveyed!",
     "recipient": "east_eve"
